      image:'/images/journal-biennale.webp',fallbackImage:'/images/journal-biennale.webp',imageAlt:'Exhibition spaces at La Biennale di Venezia',commonsQuery:'',eventDate:'8 MAY – 21 NOVEMBER 2027',
      lead:'The 20th International Architecture Exhibition is already officially scheduled from 8 May to 21 November 2027, with pre-opening days on 6 and 7 May. Wang Shu and Lu Wenyu are the curators, and the title is “Do Architecture —The possibility of coexistence in the real reality”. This early guide will be updated as pavilions, programme, tickets and visitor information are released.',
      sections:[
        ['Architecture Biennale 2027 at a glance','CONFIRMED: public dates 8 May–21 November 2027; pre-opening 6–7 May; curators Wang Shu and Lu Wenyu; main venues Giardini and Arsenale; currently published general hours 10:00–18:00; closed Mondays unless an official exception applies. 2027 tickets are not yet on sale and are currently marked as coming soon.'],
        ['Do Architecture: the 2027 theme','The official curatorial statement presents architecture as a concrete act rooted in places, materials, communities and real conditions. It explores coexistence between tradition, local knowledge, nature and innovation rather than treating architecture as an abstract or purely technological answer.'],
        ['Wang Shu and Lu Wenyu','Wang Shu and Lu Wenyu are Chinese architects known for work that pays close attention to materials, building processes and the relationship between contemporary change and the memory of place. They are the appointed curators of the 2027 International Architecture Exhibition.'],
        ['Where it takes place','The main venues are the Giardini and Arsenale. Further national participations, collateral events and venues across Venice will be added here only once the 2027 information is officially published.'],
        ['Opening hours and tickets','The current general hours are 10:00–18:00, with Mondays closed unless otherwise announced. 2027 tickets are not yet available; prices, concessions and purchase details will be added when La Biennale publishes them.'],
        ['How long to allow','Giardini and Arsenale are both extensive and content-heavy. If you want to see many pavilions, avoid squeezing everything into a few hours; splitting the visit across two sessions or days can make the experience much more manageable.'],
        ['Visiting with children','Choose a few priority sections, alternate exhibitions with outdoor breaks and keep the day flexible. Any 2027 educational activities and family services will be added when officially announced.'],
        ['Getting there','Giardini and Arsenale can be reached by vaporetto and on foot from several parts of Venice. If you are staying on the mainland, plan the trip into Venice first and then the final connection to your chosen venue.'],
        ['Driving to Venice?','Stay in Marghera, leave your car at the apartment’s free private parking and continue to Venice by bus or train rather than searching for parking at Piazzale Roma or Tronchetto on busy days.'],
        ['2027 updates','UPDATING: this guide will grow with the programme, tickets, pavilions, collateral events and practical visitor details. Unknown information will remain clearly marked instead of being copied from 2026.']
      ],
      tip:'Save the dates now, but do not plan 2027 services from 2026 information. Pavilions, ticket prices and operational details will be added only when they are official.',
